@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Terms of Use";
}
<section class="info-hero"><div class="container py-5"><span class="info-eyebrow">USING STAYNEST</span><h1>Terms of use</h1><p>Basic expectations for students, owners, and administrators using StayNest.</p></div></section>
<section class="container info-content py-5"><div class="info-card policy-copy">
    <p class="text-muted small">Last updated: October 9, 2026</p>
    <h2>1. Use of the platform</h2><p>Use StayNest lawfully and provide accurate information. Do not misuse accounts, interfere with the service, or attempt to access information that does not belong to you.</p>
    <h2>2. Student responsibilities</h2><p>Review listing details and rental terms before making a booking request. Keep communication respectful and do not submit false booking or payment information.</p>
    <h2>3. Owner responsibilities</h2><p>Provide accurate property, room, price, and availability details. Only manage listings and room records you are authorised to manage.</p>
    <h2>4. Bookings and payments</h2><p>A booking request may require owner approval. Platform status messages should be checked alongside the booking details and any applicable rental agreement. Do not treat a request as a confirmed tenancy unless the relevant confirmation is provided.</p>
    <h2>5. Content and account access</h2><p>StayNest may restrict access to accounts or content when necessary to protect users or the service. Keep your credentials confidential.</p>
    <h2>6. Support</h2><p>Questions or concerns can be sent to <a href="mailto:Admin@StayNest.com">Admin@StayNest.com</a>.</p>
    <p class="small text-muted mt-4">This is a starter terms template, not legal advice. Have it reviewed and adapted to your actual service before production use.</p>
</div></section>
